module Core

### Handle to a `suspended routine` — a stackful coroutine. Calling a `suspended routine` creates
### the coroutine AND spawns it onto this thread's implicit scheduler (it does not run yet) and
### yields one of these handles. `retrieve!()` drives the scheduler until THIS handle finishes and
### returns its value; coroutines spawned earlier on the thread progress concurrently meanwhile.
### Dropping the handle without retrieving abandons the coroutine (its cancellation shadow stack
### tears down whatever it still owned) after detaching it from the scheduler.
record Coroutine[T]
  ### The opaque coroutine handle (rf_coro*).
  secret coro: CPtr
  ### The task control block that holds the produced value (completed by the coroutine's entry thunk).
  secret result: Address

### Drives this thread's implicit scheduler until the coroutine finishes, then returns its produced
### value. Because the coroutine was spawned at the call site, a `waitfor` (or a Task await) inside
### it PARKS — the scheduler runs other coroutines meanwhile — instead of blocking. This is the
### entry into async: a program goes concurrent simply by calling suspended routines and retrieving.
### :returns: The value the suspended routine returned.
routine Coroutine[T].retrieve!() -> ?T
  if me.coro.is_none()
    throw TaskSpawnError()
  danger!
    rf_sched_run_until_default(coro: me.coro)

    var payload = rf_task_result_payload(task: me.result)
    var value = Hijacked[T](from: payload).extract()
    rf_invalidate(ptr: payload)
    return value

### Teardown: a completed coroutine is freed; one that never finished is abandoned (its shadow
### stack runs, tearing down whatever it still owns). The result task block is always released.
dangerous routine Coroutine[T].$destroy()
  if not me.coro.is_none()
    var status = rf_coro_status_get(coro: me.coro)
    if status == 3_u32                # RF_CORO_COMPLETED
      rf_coro_delete(coro: me.coro)
    else
      # Never retrieved: detach from the implicit scheduler (drop its ready/live reference) BEFORE
      # abandoning, so the scheduler does not dangle on freed memory.
      discard rf_sched_unschedule_default(coro: me.coro)
      rf_coro_abandon(coro: me.coro)
    rf_task_destroy(task: me.result)
  return
